{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251609-2e-debates-social-combat-vs-social-chase","id":1251609,"title":"[2E] Debates - Social Combat vs. Social Chase","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-05T04:08:27-07:00","id":1251609,"title":"[2E] Debates - Social Combat vs. Social Chase","content":"We now have two possible mechanics for debates scene, where PCs need to convince audience to their reasons. We got shown preview version of Social Combat rules - <i><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/guide-to-the-night-and-spilled-blood-update-vampire-the-requiem/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Lingua Bellum</b></a></i> - from the Vampire's <b>Guide to Night</b>. From <b>CoD Rulebook</b> we have on <i>Chase Rules</i> implication it can be used for Social scenes, where 'chase' is to convince audience.<br /> <br /> Topic is to gauge what is better mechanics for which scenes. In my point of view, Social Combat looks as a bit too complex to running it on high emotional scenes, but it's probably my own test. On the other hand, Social Chase has no prepared stakes, traits limits, etc.<br /> <br /> I may steal some complications from Social Combat to gauge Social Chase thresholds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-05-2018, 07:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T09:27:05-07:00","id":1251685,"title":"","content":"In my opinion it depends on the situation. If it's a clandestine meeting between 2 vampires having a conversation on taking territory and how to share it, or how to approach combat, take the chase option <br /> <br /> If it's something like going against a carthian rebellion orator as an agent of the invictus in Elysium, take the lingua bellium option","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T08:00:48-07:00","id":1254207,"title":"","content":"I'd do chase if it is to convince a group of people of something they were uninterested in or kinda meh about, combat when two different points of view clash.<br /> Talking about evolution on a school event is very different from talking about evolution on live-tv in a debate with creationists as Bill Nye did, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}